   "q": "Harbour Shipping Ltd (an English company) and Lyon Freight SA (a French company) signed a contract stating that it is governed by French law. It contains a clause referring all disputes to arbitration seated in London, but says nothing about the law governing the arbitration clause itself. A dispute arose and Harbour Shipping commenced arbitration in October 2025. Lyon Freight argues the arbitration clause is invalid under French law.\n\nWhich law governs the validity of the arbitration agreement?",
