   "e": "The correct advice is that **the court may order mediation and may penalise an unreasonable refusal in costs, even if she wins**.\n- Following **Churchill v Merthyr Tydfil CBC [2023]**, the CPR were amended from **1 October 2024**: the overriding objective includes **promoting or using ADR**, and the court can **order** parties to engage in ADR.\n- On costs, the court considers **unreasonable failure to engage** in ADR or failure to comply with an ADR order, using factors such as those in **Halsey**. Confidence in winning is rarely a good reason.\n\nMediation is no longer purely voluntary once ordered. Strike-out and automatic indemnity costs overstate the sanctions; the penalty is discretionary, usually a reduction in recoverable costs. No pre-action protocol requirement is needed."
