   "e": "**No contract: the display was an invitation to treat.**\n- Goods displayed in shop windows or on shelves are **invitations to treat**, not offers (**Fisher v Bell**, **Pharmaceutical Society v Boots**).\n- Mira made the **offer** at the till, which the manager was free to **reject**. No acceptance means no contract.\n\nWhy the others are wrong:\n- The display was not an offer, so Mira could not accept it, and the shop is not bound by the advertised price.\n- The court will not create a contract at £850; nothing was agreed at that price.\n- Unilateral mistake (Hartog v Colin and Shields) is irrelevant because no contract was ever formed."
