   "q": "Kestrel Developments contracted with Owain, a joiner, to fit out 20 flats for £40,000. Halfway through, Owain told Kestrel he was in financial difficulty and might not finish. Kestrel faced a penalty under its own contract with the building owner if the flats were late, so it promised Owain an extra £500 per completed flat. Owain completed the work on time. Kestrel now refuses to pay the extra money, saying Owain only did what he was already bound to do. There was no threat or pressure from Owain.\n\nWhich of the following best describes Kestrel's promise?",
