   "q": "Sam attends a hospital A&E department with severe stomach pains late at night. The doctor on duty negligently refuses to examine him and sends him home. Sam dies later that night of arsenic poisoning. Expert evidence shows that, even with prompt examination, Sam would almost certainly have died because no antidote could have been given in time.\n\nWhich of the following best explains why the hospital is not liable for Sam's death?",
