   "e": "The IHT is **£180,000**.\n- The home passes to **Lisa**, a **direct descendant**, so the **residence nil rate band** applies. It is limited to the lower of the RNRB (£175,000) and the home's value (£450,000), so **£175,000**.\n- The estate is under £2 million, so there is no taper.\n- Nil rate bands available: £325,000 + £175,000 = £500,000.\n- Chargeable: £950,000 - £500,000 = £450,000. Tax at 40% is **£180,000**.\n- £250,000 is the figure if you leave out the RNRB.\n- Kemal was never married, so there is no transferable NRB. The share Mo takes does not affect the RNRB, which depends only on the home going to Lisa."
