   "e": "The correct answer is to **refuse**.\n\n- **Rule 3.3**: a client account must **not** be used to **provide banking facilities** to clients or third parties. Payments in and out must be **in respect of the delivery of regulated services**.\n- Receiving and passing on funds that have nothing to do with the legal work is a classic banking facility. It is also a **money laundering** red flag (unexplained third-party overseas funds), so the firm should consider whether a report to its MLRO is needed.\n\nChecking the invoice, paying promptly or using a designated account does not change the purpose of the payment. Charging a fee would not make it a regulated service; it would make the breach worse."
