   "e": "The correct answer is that **Mia has one third** as a tenant in common and **Leo has two thirds**.\n\n- Jack's sale of his own beneficial share was an **act operating on his own share** (**Williams v Hensman**). It severed **only his** share, so Mia took a **one-third share as tenant in common**.\n- Kemi and Leo remained **joint tenants** of the other two thirds between themselves.\n- On Kemi's death, **survivorship** operated, so Leo took the whole of the two-thirds joint tenancy.\n\nKemi's estate gets nothing because she was still a joint tenant. Mia does not need to hold the legal estate to have a beneficial interest. Severance by one joint tenant does not turn every interest into a tenancy in common."
