   "q": "Pavel owns a house and a field. He sells the field to Quinn. For years Pavel walked across the field along a clearly worn track to reach a lane, which is the only practical access to the field from the lane, although the field also has a separate gate to a main road. The transfer to Quinn is silent about easements. Pavel now claims he can still use the track to reach the lane from his house.\n\nWhich of the following best describes Pavel's position?",
