 "cards": [
  [
   "What are the seven SRA Principles?",
   "Act: 1 upholding **rule of law** and administration of justice; 2 upholding **public trust**; 3 with **independence**; 4 with **honesty**; 5 with **integrity**; 6 encouraging **EDI**; 7 in **best interests of each client**."
  ],
  [
   "When two SRA Principles conflict, which ones take precedence?",
   "Those protecting the **wider public interest** (rule of law, public confidence, duty to court) **prevail** over the client's interests."
  ],
  [
   "What are the four areas of the Statement of Solicitor Competence?",
   "**A** Ethics, professionalism and judgement; **B** Technical legal practice; **C** Working with other people; **D** Managing themselves and their own work."
  ],
  [
   "What counts as an undertaking under the SRA definition?",
   "A statement, **oral or written**, whether or not it says \"undertake\", to someone who **reasonably relies** on it, that you **will** (or will not) do something."
  ],
  [
   "What are the key rules on performing and releasing an undertaking?",
   "Personal and binds firm; perform within agreed or **reasonable time**; client cannot override; only recipient can release; court can enforce."
  ],
  [
   "If a client admits guilt but pleads not guilty, what can and can't their solicitor do at trial?",
   "**Can**: put prosecution to proof, cross-examine, submit no case. **Cannot**: assert innocence, blame someone else, call false evidence."
  ],
  [
   "What must a solicitor do if a client insists on misleading the court?",
   "**Cease to act**; tell court only \"**professional reasons**\"; keep the reason confidential."
  ],
  [
   "What does Code para 2.7 require a solicitor to draw to the court's attention?",
   "Draw the court's attention to **relevant cases, statutes and procedural irregularities**, even if adverse to your client."
  ],
  [
   "What is the test for lack of capacity under the Mental Capacity Act 2005?",
   "Presumed capacity. Lacks it if, due to **impairment of mind or brain**, cannot **understand, retain, use or weigh, communicate**. Decision-specific."
  ],
  [
   "What must a solicitor do when a third party gives instructions on behalf of a client?",
   "Confirm directly with the **client** (ideally alone); check **authority**, **capacity** and no **undue influence**; keep confidentiality."
  ],
  [
   "When can a firm transfer its costs from client account to business account?",
   "Only after a **bill or written notification** of costs is given to the client."
  ],
  [
   "What is the banking facility ban in the SRA Accounts Rules?",
   "Client account only for payments relating to **regulated legal services**. Return money promptly when no proper reason to hold it."
  ],
  [
   "What must a solicitor ensure when a client is referred by an introducer or there is fee sharing (Code para 5.1)?",
   "Tell client of **interest** and **fee sharing**; fee sharing **in writing**; no referral payments in **criminal** cases; client not acquired improperly. PI referral fees banned (LASPO)."
  ],
  [
   "What does Code para 8.9 prohibit on unsolicited approaches, and who is exempt?",
   "No unsolicited approaches to **members of the public** to advertise, except **current or former clients**."
  ],
  [
   "What is an own interest conflict, and can client consent cure it?",
   "Your interest conflicts with client's (or significant risk). **No exceptions**, consent irrelevant. Includes significant **gifts**."
  ],
  [
   "What are the two exceptions to the client conflict rule in Code para 6.2, and what conditions must also be met?",
   "**Substantially common interest** or **competing for same objective**, PLUS: informed **written** consent, **safeguards** for confidentiality, **reasonable** to act."
  ],
  [
   "What are the four exceptions to the duty of disclosure in Code para 6.4?",
   "(a) **legal restriction** (national security/crime prevention, e.g. tipping off); (b) client's **written consent**; (c) **serious injury** risk; (d) **mistakenly disclosed privileged** document."
  ],
  [
   "When can a solicitor act against a former client whose confidential information they hold (Code para 6.5)?",
   "Not if you hold their **material confidential information** unless **effective measures** (no real risk) or their informed **written consent**."
  ],
  [
   "What do Code paras 7.7 and 7.8 require a solicitor to report to the SRA?",
   "Report promptly facts you **reasonably believe** capable of a **serious breach** by anyone regulated (incl. you); and inform the SRA of matters it should **investigate**."
  ],
  [
   "What must a solicitor notify the SRA of under Code para 7.6?",
   "Notify SRA promptly of **criminal charge, conviction or caution**; **insolvency** event; **material changes** or **false/inaccurate** information given to the SRA."
  ],
  [
   "What must a solicitor do when things go wrong on a client's matter (Code para 7.11)?",
   "Be **honest and open**, **put matters right**, explain fully and promptly. Own interest conflict: advise **independent advice**, notify **insurers**."
  ],
  [
   "What are the Legal Ombudsman time limits for bringing a complaint?",
   "Complain to firm first; LeO after **final response** or **8 weeks**; refer within **6 months** of final response; and within **1 year** of act/omission or **1 year** of awareness."
  ],
  [
   "What remedies can the Legal Ombudsman award, and what is the cap?",
   "Apology, fee refund or reduction, compensation, putting things right. Cap **£50,000**. Binding if complainant accepts."
  ],
  [
   "Under the SRA warning notice, what disclosures must an NDA not prevent?",
   "Reporting to **SRA/regulators**, **police**, **protected disclosures**, disclosures **required by law**, or to own advisers. Void for crime victims (s.17 VPA 2024)."
  ],
  [
   "What are the red flags and improper tactics identified in the SRA SLAPPs warning notice?",
   "**Public interest** publication; **power imbalance**; **meritless** or oppressive claim. Tactics: exaggerated threats, short deadlines, misusing \"**without prejudice**\"/\"**not for publication**\"."
  ]
 ]
