   "body": "- Liable: **Lister v Hesley Hall** (2001): boarding house warden abused boys in his care; **Mohamud v WM Morrison** (2016): kiosk attendant followed a customer out and attacked him in an unbroken sequence; **Bellman v Northampton Recruitment** (2018): managing director punched an employee while asserting his authority\n- Not liable: **WM Morrison v Various Claimants** (2020): auditor leaked payroll data in a personal vendetta; **BXB** (2023): Jehovah's Witness elder raped a member at his home: mere opportunity\n- Job done in a prohibited or careless way: liable (**Limpus v London General Omnibus** (1862): bus driver raced a rival; **Century Insurance** (1942): tanker driver lit a cigarette while delivering petrol; **Rose v Plenty** (1976): milkman let a boy help against orders)\n- Own purposes or a frolic: not liable (**Twine v Bean's Express** (1946): forbidden lift to a hitchhiker; **Hilton v Thomas Burton** (1961): workmen drove to a café on an unauthorised break)\n!! \"The employer told him not to\" is no defence on its own: ask whose purposes the act served",
